{"text": "Mark BRNOVICH OFFICE OF THE ATTORNEY GENERAL\n\nATTORNEY GENERAL STATE OF ARIZONA\n\nJune 3, 2020\nThe Honorable Doug Ducey The Honorable Karen Fann The Honorable Rusty Bowers\n1700 W. Washington St. 1700 W. Washington St. 1700 W. Washington St.\nPhoenix, AZ 85007 Phoenix, AZ 85007 Phoenix, AZ 85007\n\nDear Governor Ducey, President Fann, and Speaker Bowers:\n\nWe have all watched the video of George Floyd with shock and outrage. As Arizona\u2019s\ntop law enforcement official, I hope Mr. Floyd\u2019s death will not be in vain but will serve as a\ncatalyst for positive reforms.\n\nOver the past several years the Attorney General\u2019s Office has provided de-escalation and\ncultural diversity training for our sworn agents. Although the Arizona Peace Officer Standards\nand Training Board offers training on these topics, they are not mandated. The time has come to\nrequire all law enforcement agencies to have robust de-escalation training that is regularly\nadministered. Let\u2019s work together to set a new standard for Arizona\u2019s law enforcement training.\n\nIn addition, it is imperative that we maintain public confidence in the investigations\nfollowing officer-involved shootings and excessive use of force. Arizona should ensure a third\nparty oversees these matters. One option would be to designate the Attorney General to oversee\nthese investigations as has been done in California and New York, and I would support that for\nArizona. There are also other viable options to consider.\n\nFinally, Arizona should pursue additional outreach programs by law enforcement to our\ncommunities, especially our younger generation. Whether it\u2019s a \u201cKnow Your Rights\u201d campaign,\nor classroom presentations, it is clear that more needs to be done. Our office has some\ncompelling ideas on where Arizona should go from here, and we look forward to working with\nyou to bring these programs to fruition.\n\nGoodness can come from even the worst situations. Let\u2019s honor the sincere concerns of\nthe people we serve and advance the cause of justice.\n\nRespectfully,\n\nMark Brnovich\n\n2005 NortH Centra Avenue, PHOENIX, ARIZONA 85004 \u00a2 PHONE 602.542.4266 \u00a9 Fax 602.542.4085 \u00a9 www.azaG.co\\",
"words": [
